Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(secure-connect): split tunneling (bypass
 apps/subnets) + settings UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- SingboxRoutingService: GenRoutingSplitTunnel() adds sing-box `direct` route
  rules for KillSwitchItem.BypassApps (process_name/process_path) and
  BypassSubnets (ip_cidr). Placed after the TUN anti-loop reject and the core's
  own direct rules but before the generic DNS hijack and final proxy, so a
  bypassed process also resolves DNS directly and egresses on the physical NIC.
  Mode: tunnel everything except the lists — consistent with the kill switch,
  which permits the same lists through the firewall.
- OptionSettingViewModel: EnableKillSwitch, KillSwitchAllowLan,
  KillSwitchBypassApps, KillSwitchBypassSubnets — loaded in Init, persisted in
  SaveSettingAsync.
- Avalonia OptionSettingWindow: new "Kill Switch" tab (toggles + split-tunnel
  lists) bound to the view model.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
